  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "This is a patch release with a list-parsing behavioral change, a CSS fix for embedded usage (ToHtml).\n\n## Markdown list parsing (behavioral change)\n\nList markers now always interrupt a paragraph, matching the CommonMark spec in practice:\n\n- Any ordered list marker may interrupt a paragraph: any start number (not only 1.) starts a list, instead of lazy-continuing the open paragraph (documented deviation, spec example 303).\n- Unordered list markers may interrupt a paragraph as well, including a marker without content.\n- A list marker line ends a blockquote: the marker interrupts the quoted paragraph, so the quote closes and the list is parsed in the outer scope.\n- The redundant in-list relaxation of the paragraph-interruption rule has been removed.\n- WouldStartBlockquoteBreakingConstruct now accepts the ')' ordered delimiter in addition to '.'.\n\n## ToHtml CSS fix\n\nThe document layout (max-width, margin, padding) moved from the body element to a .markdown-document wrapper div, so the shared CSS no longer constrains embedded or iframe usage. ToHtmlDocument output now includes a .markdown-document wrapper around the content.",
